<exercise>
  <title>NN: Computing number parameter to fit  <m>Y</m></title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      For each of the following NN architectures, determine the number of parameters that need to be fit. 
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <task>
  <statement>
    <p>A classification NN with the following:<ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          Input layer: <m>p=784</m> units.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Hidden layer 1: <m>K_1=256</m> units.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Hidden layer 2: <m>K_2=128</m> units.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Output layer: <m>C=10</m> units.
        </p>
      </li>
      </ul></p>
  </statement>
  <hint>
    <p>
      <md>
  <mrow>A_{k}^{(1)} \amp= h_{k}^{(1)}(X)</mrow>
  <mrow>\amp= g(w_{k0}^{(1)} + \sum_{j=1}^{p} w_{kj}^{(1)} X_j)</mrow>
</md>

      <md>
  <mrow>A_{\ell}^{(2)} \amp= h_{\ell}^{(2)}(X)</mrow>
  <mrow>\amp= g(w_{\ell 0}^{(2)} + \sum_{k=1}^{K_1} w_{\ell k}^{(2)} A_k^{(1)})</mrow>
</md>
<md>
  <mrow>Z_m \amp= \beta_{m0} + \sum_{\ell=1}^{K_2} \beta_{m\ell} h_{\ell}^{(2)}(X)</mrow>
  <mrow>\amp= \beta_{m0} + \sum_{\ell=1}^{K_2} \beta_{m\ell} A_{\ell}^{(2)},</mrow>
</md>


    </p>
  </hint>
  <solution>
    <p>
      For the first hidden layer, we have <m>1+p</m> weights to fit per unit in <m>L_1</m>. For <m>K_1=256</m> units, we have to fit
      <md>
        K_1(1+p)=256(1+784)=200,960.
      </md>
      
    </p>
    <p>
      For the second hidden layer, we have <m>1+K_1</m> weights to fit per unit in <m>L_2</m>. For <m>K_2=128</m> units, we have to fit
      <md>
        K_2(1+K_1)=128(1+256)=32,896.
      </md>
    </p>
    <p>
      For the output layer, we have <m>1+K_2</m> weights to fit per output unit. For <m>C=10</m> output units, we need to fit
      <md>
        C(1+K_2)=10(1+128)=1290
      </md>
      Therefore, the total number of weights we need to fit is
      <md>
        K_1(1+p) + K_2(1+K_1) + C(1+K_2) =200,960 + 32,896 + 1290= 235,146       
      </md>
    </p>
  </solution>
  </task>
</exercise>



