<exercise xml:id="ex-rgb-convolution">
  <title>CNN: 3-Channel (RGB) Convolution Calculation</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Suppose we apply a single <m>2 \times 2 \times 3</m> convolutional filter to a <m>2 \times 2</m> RGB image.
    </p>
    <p>
      The three <m>2 \times 2</m> input channels (<m>X_R, X_G, X_B</m>) and corresponding convolution filters (<m>K_R, K_G, K_B</m>) are given by:
    
    <md>
      <mrow>
        X_R \amp= \begin{bmatrix} 2 \amp 1 \\ 0 \amp 3 \end{bmatrix}, \amp
        X_G \amp= \begin{bmatrix} 1 \amp 4 \\ 2 \amp 0 \end{bmatrix}, \amp
        X_B \amp= \begin{bmatrix} 3 \amp 0 \\ 1 \amp 2 \end{bmatrix}
      </mrow>
      <mrow>
        K_R \amp= \begin{bmatrix} 1 \amp 0 \\ -1 \amp 2 \end{bmatrix}, \amp
        K_G \amp= \begin{bmatrix} 0 \amp 1 \\ 1 \amp -1 \end{bmatrix}, \amp
        K_B \amp= \begin{bmatrix} -1 \amp 2 \\ 0 \amp 1 \end{bmatrix}
      </mrow>
    </md>
    </p>
    <p>
      Answer the following questions.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <task>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Compute the individual convolved images for the Red, Green, and Blue channels: <m>(X_R * K_R)</m>, <m>(X_G * K_G)</m>, and <m>(X_B * K_B)</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    <solution>
      <p>
        Multiply corresponding entries element-by-element and sum the results for each channel:
      
      <md>
        <mrow>X_R * K_R \amp= (2)(1) + (1)(0) + (0)(-1) + (3)(2) = 2 + 0 + 0 + 6 = 8</mrow>
        <mrow>X_G * K_G \amp= (1)(0) + (4)(1) + (2)(1) + (0)(-1) = 0 + 4 + 2 + 0 = 6</mrow>
        <mrow>X_B * K_B \amp= (3)(-1) + (0)(2) + (1)(0) + (2)(1) = -3 + 0 + 0 + 2 = -1</mrow>
      </md>
      and the colvolved image in each channel is just a scalar.
      </p>
    </solution>
  </task>

  <task>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Combine the three channel outputs. 
      </p>
    </statement>
    <solution>
      <p>
        Sum the three channel results element-wise:
      
      <md>
        z = 8 + 6 + (-1) = 13
      </md>
      </p>      
    </solution>
  </task>
  <task>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Add the bias <m>b = -1</m>, and apply the ReLU activation function to find the final output pixel <m>Y(1,1)</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    <solution>
      <p>
      Sum the three channel results together with the bias <m>b = -1</m>:
      
      <md>
        z = 8 + 6 + (-1) + (-1) = 13 + (-1) = 12
      </md>
      </p>
      <p>
        Apply the ReLU activation function <m>g(z) = \max(0, z)</m>:
      
      <md>
        Y(1,1) = \max(0, 12) = 12
      </md>
      </p>
    </solution>
  </task>
</exercise>




